        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5841a0bb-98d2-5d88-a154-955e5cdd8a84",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bossiaea, Ferraria, Platylobium, Platylobium infecundum\n- Families: Fabaceae, Iridaceae\n- People: James Edward Smith\n- Concepts: plant genera, species relationships, native ranges\n\nFacts:\n- James Edward Smith first described the genus Platylobium.\n- Bossiaea is a genus in the pea family Fabaceae with about 70 species native to Australia.\n- Ferraria is a genus of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family Iridaceae that is native to tropical and southern Africa.\n- Platylobium is closely allied to Bossiaea within the Mirbelioids.\n- Platylobium infecundum is a species in the genus Platylobium and the family Fabaceae.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
